{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:811e8319813d4dc5","name":"Holster","source":{"id":"source:reference-811e8319813d4dc5","title":"Holster","revision":18255,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T19:51:21Z","sha256":"cd7e2cc61d64a744ea47bbf0cae57ce0b46bea1596a0b539a173a16d481546ba","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18255","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Holster&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-811e8319813d4dc5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["HOLSTER\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEIGHT\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Hip\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0.5 kg\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Concealed\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["50\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0.2 kg\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Holsters are generally available for all Medium or smaller weapons. (Larger weapons are usually carried on shoulder straps, hangers, or baldrics that cost as much as a Hip Holster.) A Holster for a melee weapon is usually called a sheath.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Hip Holster:"]}," This Holster holds the weapon in an easily accessed- and easily seen- location."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Concealed Holster:"]}," A Concealed Holster is designed to help keep a weapon out of sight. On most cases, this is a Shoulder Holster (the weapon fits under the wearer's armpit, presumably beneath a jacket, vest, or cloak). Small or Tiny weapons and single-bladed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," can be carried in concealed waistband holsters (often placed inside the wearer's waistband in the small of the back). Tiny weapons and single-bladed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," can also be carried on ankle, boot, or wrist Holsters.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["A Concealed Holster allows you to draw a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concealed Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concealed_Weapon"}," as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},", instead of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},", but you take a -5 penalty on your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," check to conceal the weapon."]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
